# jasmin/ADMITS
# =============
#
# Every declaration that could leave a proof unfinished or add an
# assumption in the Rocq development of the pinned Jasmin commit, as found
# by build.sh (`Admitted.`,
# `admit.`, `Abort.`, `Axiom`, `Parameter`, `Hypothesis`, `Conjecture`, with
# `Local`/`Global` forms), one per line: file, keyword, first word of the
# declaration. build.sh stops if the scan
# differs from this list, so any new such declaration is a reviewed change.
#
# None is `Admitted`, `admit` or `Abort`. The `Parameter` and `Axiom`
# declarations of arch_extra.v, expr.v, gen_map.v, ident.v, memory_model.v,
# tagged.v, unionfind.v and varmap.v are fields of module types, provided by
# the modules that implement them; the `Hypothesis` declarations are section
# hypotheses, discharged when their section closes. The global ones
# are label.v (encoding of code labels: encode_label, decode_label and the
# axiom decode_encode_label) and waes.v (MixColumns, InvMixColumns); they
# appear in the assumption report (ASSUMPTIONS).
#
# Upstream main at JASMIN_BASE has 168 of these entries. The topics add
# four, all from the safety pass and its soundness proof (carried from
# jasmin-lang/jasmin#1572), and of the two kinds above: the fields
# get_totalE, getP_mode and get_eq_mode of the module type VM in varmap.v,
# implemented by its module Vm, and the section hypothesis
# get_global_arr_init of toEC/safety_proof.v.

